"""AskTheDB evaluation set: 100 questions over the Chinook database.

Each case is a dict:
    id        unique id (E = easy, M = medium, H = hard, X = edge, A = ambiguous, O = out of scope)
    category  easy | medium | hard | edge | ambiguous | out_of_scope
    lang      zh | en
    dims      SQL dimensions the question exercises
    question  the question sent to the workflow
    expect    answer         -> must answer correctly (compared with the gold SQL)
              clarify_or_assume -> must ask for clarification, or answer with a stated interpretation
              reject         -> must refuse or clarify, and must not run any SQL
    sql       gold SQL (for expect == answer)
    check     column indexes of the gold result that must appear in the answer (default: all)
    tol       numeric tolerance when matching numbers in the answer (default 0.011)
    accept    alternative values; the answer passes if it contains any of them
    signless  match numbers by absolute value (for answers that say 'decreased by X')
    clarify_ok  also pass if the workflow stops with a clarification or an explanation (clarify / reject)
"""

